# SIS Core Conventions

Read `.cursor/brain/PROJECT.md` for full context.

## Stack
Laravel 13 + Inertia/React + PostgreSQL + Redis. Reference architecture in `.cursor/architecture/`.

## Non-Negotiable Rules
1. Every academic operation scoped to `academic_year_id`
2. Never hard-delete official academic records — use status + effective_to
3. Heavy ops (bulk import, certificates, reports) via Laravel Queue — never in HTTP request
4. PostgreSQL = source of truth; Redis = cache only
5. No manual DB changes — always versioned migrations
6. No `SELECT *` in production API queries
7. No N+1 queries — eager load relationships
8. Idempotency keys for payments, imports, certificates, notifications
9. Correlation ID on every request for audit tracing
10. Measure slow queries with EXPLAIN ANALYZE before adding indexes

## Data Types (PostgreSQL)
- PKs: `BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY`
- Status: `SMALLINT` (not TINYINT)
- Money: `NUMERIC(12,2)`
- Timestamps: `TIMESTAMPTZ`

## Module Implementation Order
organization → academic → security → students → enrollment → curriculum → teachers → attendance → exams → lifecycle modules

## Database Changes — MANDATORY
Any create/alter/index/delete/improvement to the database MUST follow:
1. `.cursor/skills/database-change/SKILL.md` — read and execute full workflow
2. `.cursor/architecture/DATABASE-CHANGE-CHECKLIST.md` — complete every item
3. Update `.cursor/architecture/database-blueprint.md` after every schema change

Never skip reference files. Never change schema without updating blueprint.

## Database Blueprint
Table definitions: `.cursor/architecture/database-blueprint.md` — source of truth for schema design.
